  Values:
    Speaker: ""
    Portrait: 0
    Lines:
      - Speaker: ""
        Text: Ah, the shrine maiden. So the tremor reached the mountain too. It cracked the old arch under our bridge.
      - Speaker: ""
        Text: Last night the well hummed. Low and steady, like the bell at your shrine. Seventy years, and I never heard it do that.
      - Speaker: ""
        Text: If the old monk sent you down, he fears what I fear. Look to the bridge, and the stones beneath it.
